      "content": "Text A is a clear example of how white-collar professionalism is often coded as \"correct\" and \"safe,\" while Text B's grammatical errors and slang reveal a lack of the polished veneer expected in corporate hierarchies. Text A scores a 9/10 for professionalism and executive presence because it uses standard, non-threatening language that aligns with traditional power structures, whereas Text B scores a 3/10 due to its unpolished tone. Text A sounds significantly more like a leader because it projects the controlled, authoritative demeanor that is culturally associated with successful executives.",
